       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose, so it could cause severe, prolonged hypotension and shock. The problem is the dose, and a non-clinician's confirmation doesn't address it. The prescribing clinician has to decide on the dose.\n\nHere are the options:\n- **Prescriber enters it:** the treating physician can enter the order directly. Pharmacy will review it, and that review is the safeguard for an unusual dose.\n- **Dose correction:** if 5 mg or 10 mg once daily was intended, tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Clinical question:** if the goal is stronger blood pressure control, the prescriber or pharmacist can suggest safer options. These include adding another drug class.\n\nI'm happy to enter a corrected order as soon as I have one."
      }
